  <section class="ll-sec" id="faq">
    <div class="ll-wn">
      <div class="ll-sec-hd center">
        <span class="ll-kicker">Help Center</span>
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="ll-faq-list">

        <div class="ll-faq"><div class="ll-faq-q"><span>How does LitterLoops™ work?</span><svg class="ll-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div><div class="ll-faq-a">You manually turn the drum once. The internal sieve catches solid clumps and directs them into the collection drawer while clean litter filters back through. Slide the drawer out, discard, slide back in.</div></div>

        <div class="ll-faq"><div class="ll-faq-q"><span>Does it require electricity or batteries?</span><svg class="ll-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div><div class="ll-faq-a">No. LitterLoops™ does not require electricity, a charging cable, wall outlet, or batteries of any kind. It is entirely manual.</div></div>

        <div class="ll-faq"><div class="ll-faq-q"><span>What type of litter must I use?</span><svg class="ll-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div><div class="ll-faq-a">You must use a fine-grain clumping litter (clay, corn, cassava, or similar). The sieve depends on solid clumps forming. Non-clumping litters, large wood pellets, paper pellets, and non-clumping crystals will not work with this mechanism.</div></div>

        <div class="ll-faq"><div class="ll-faq-q"><span>Can large cats use it?</span><svg class="ll-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div><div class="ll-faq-a">Please check the confirmed dimensions in the product listing or on the packaging. If your cat is a large breed (Maine Coon, Ragdoll, Norwegian Forest Cat), we strongly recommend verifying interior dimensions before purchasing.</div></div>

        <div class="ll-faq"><div class="ll-faq-q"><span>Will the drum move while my cat is inside?</span><svg class="ll-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div><div class="ll-faq-a">No. The drum only rotates when you manually turn it. It does not spin automatically or from your cat's weight. The base cradle holds the drum fixed during use.</div></div>

        <div class="ll-faq"><div class="ll-faq-q"><span>Does rotating it create a lot of dust?</span><svg class="ll-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div><div class="ll-faq-a">Some dust movement is possible, as with any litter disturbance. Rotating slowly and using a low-dust clumping litter brand minimizes this significantly.</div></div>

        <div class="ll-faq"><div class="ll-faq-q"><span>How often should I empty the waste drawer?</span><svg class="ll-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div><div class="ll-faq-a">For a single cat: every 3–7 days. For multiple cats: every 2–3 days. The included guide provides more specific guidance.</div></div>

        <div class="ll-faq"><div class="ll-faq-q"><span>Does it eliminate odor?</span><svg class="ll-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div><div class="ll-faq-a">LitterLoops™ has an open design. It moves waste into the collection drawer, which helps reduce surface odor. It does not seal or eliminate odors — regular daily rotation and an odor-control clumping litter are your most effective tools.</div></div>

        <div class="ll-faq"><div class="ll-faq-q"><span>Do I still need to manually clean the box?</span><svg class="ll-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div><div class="ll-faq-a">Yes. LitterLoops™ simplifies daily waste removal but does not replace periodic basin cleaning. Occasional manual rinsing and spot-cleaning are still part of normal maintenance.</div></div>

        <div class="ll-faq"><div class="ll-faq-q"><span>How do I clean the unit?</span><svg class="ll-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div><div class="ll-faq-a">Because there are no electrical components, the drum and drawer can be detached, rinsed with warm water and pet-safe soap, and air-dried. See the included care guide for a full cleaning procedure.</div></div>

        <div class="ll-faq"><div class="ll-faq-q"><span>My cat might refuse to use it. What then?</span><svg class="ll-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div><div class="ll-faq-a">Most cats adapt to new litter boxes when the transition is gradual — place LitterLoops™ next to the existing box with the same litter type, and let your cat explore on its own timeline. The open, familiar format helps. If your cat does not adapt, contact our support team to discuss your options.</div></div>

        <div class="ll-faq"><div class="ll-faq-q"><span>How long does shipping take?</span><svg class="ll-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div><div class="ll-faq-a">Please check your order confirmation email or our store shipping policy page for accurate estimates to your location.</div></div>

        <div class="ll-faq"><div class="ll-faq-q"><span>What is the return policy?</span><svg class="ll-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div><div class="ll-faq-a">Please visit our store's return policy page or contact our customer support team for full details on returns and refunds.</div></div>

      </div>
